.nh
.TH "PVEFORGE" "1" "Sep 2026" "pveforge" "pveforge manual"

.SH NAME
pveforge-acl-grant - Grant a role on a path to a user, group or token


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpveforge acl grant <target-id> (--user <userid> | --group <groupid> | --token <tokenid>) --grant PATH:ROLE[:PRIVS[:PROPAGATE]]\&... [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Grant a role on a path to a user, group or token, as root over SSH with pveum
acl modify. The roster's API token never holds Permissions.Modify.

.PP
--grant PATH:ROLE[:PRIVS[:PROPAGATE]] is repeatable, as for bootstrap:
PROPAGATE is 0 unless given as 1, and PRIVS, when given, must be exactly the
role's privileges on PVE.

.PP
Refused before anything is granted:
  - a grant to the roster's own token, to the user that owns it, or to a
    group that user is in (always; there is no override);
  - a role conferring an escalating privilege (Permissions.Modify, User.Modify, Sys.Modify, Realm.Allocate, Sys.Console, VM.Monitor, Realm.AllocateUser, Datastore.Allocate, Mapping.Modify),
    unless --allow-escalating-role is given;
  - an unknown role, a role with no privileges, or PRIVS that differ from
    the role's.

.PP
The ACL list is read back afterwards as root, and each grant's exact entry
(path, role, principal, propagate) must be in it. PVE merges a repeated
grant, so repeating one changes nothing there. A grant cannot be undone by
pveforge: revoke it with pveum acl delete.

.PP
The checks hold only for the roles, groups and users as read just before the
grant. A grant to a group reaches every member, including one who joins
later; a role widened (pveum role modify) after the grant widens it. Nothing
serialises acl grant against user ensure, or either against changes made
outside pveforge.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--allow-escalating-role\fP[=false]
	allow a role conferring an escalating privilege: Permissions.Modify, User.Modify, Sys.Modify, Realm.Allocate, Sys.Console, VM.Monitor, Realm.AllocateUser, Datastore.Allocate, Mapping.Modify

.PP
\fB--grant\fP=[]
	a grant PATH:ROLE[:PRIVS[:PROPAGATE]] (repeatable; PROPAGATE defaults to 0)

.PP
\fB--group\fP=""
	grant to this group

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for grant

.PP
\fB--no-ssh-key\fP[=false]
	connect as root with the PVE password (PVEFORGE_PVE_PASSWORD, else a prompt) for this run only, trusting the host key on first use, as bootstrap --no-ssh-key does; required for a target that holds no SSH key

.PP
\fB--roster\fP=""
	path to the roster file (overrides PVEFORGE_ROSTER and the default ./pveforge.toml)

.PP
\fB--token\fP=""
	grant to this API token (<name>@<realm>!<tokenname>)

.PP
\fB--user\fP=""
	grant to this user (<name>@<realm>)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpveforge-acl(1)\fP
